

Sample answer

Subject: Request to repair heating this week

Dear [Landlord’s name],

I hope you are well. I am writing to ask whether the heating in the apartment can be repaired this week. The apartment has been cold for several days, and it is becoming uncomfortable, especially at night.

Could you please let me know when a technician can come? I would be grateful if you could arrange the repair as soon as possible.

Thank you for your time and attention.

Kind regards,
[Your name]

User may adapt the email to their own situation.

Grammar explanation

The email uses polite requests such as “Could you please let me know…?” and “I would be grateful if you could arrange…”. These are softer than direct commands. The phrase “has been cold for several days” uses the present perfect continuous to show a situation that started in the past and continues now. “Can be repaired” uses the passive voice because the focus is on the repair, not on who will repair it.

Vocabulary highlights

  • repair: to fix something that is broken
  • technician: a person who repairs equipment
  • uncomfortable: not pleasant or
